# App composition + main loop for the walker example.
#
# Structure (see docs/app-systems-architecture.md): an `App` owns per-system
# state structs; `createApp` builds them, `runWalkerApp` drives the loop, and
# `updateApp` / `renderApp` sequence the systems. Each system lives in its own
# sibling file, all merging into one module:
#   ui.rae (uiUpdate) · camera.rae (cameraUpdate) · character.rae + hud.rae ·
#   terrain.rae · grass.rae · render.rae (the render-graph walk) ·
#   physics.rae (fixed-step seam) · net.rae (multiplayer seam) · state.rae
#   (hot-reload + window persistence).
# app.rae keeps the App / state types, createApp, the loop, updateApp, frameBegin.
# Still to come: the input-intent split (#545) and turning the single character
# into a multiplayer-ready roster (#546/#547).
